      "writtenOn": "2024-01-19T09:33:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think that if this gets called with FORWARD_NONE, and an iifName which has never been added to mPhysicalInterfaceNameMap, then getInterfaceIndex will return null and this will crash because null can\u0027t be cast to int.\n\nNot sure if this can happen though. It looks like for it to happen, oldConfig would have to have FORWARD_NONE but oldConfig.equals(newConfig) would have to return true. I\u0027m not sure if it\u0027s possible to construct such an object.\n\nFor safety I suppose you could do:\n\n    Integer iifIndex \u003d getInterfaceIndex(iifName);\n    if (iifIndex \u003d\u003d null) {\n        // This cannot happen unless the new config has FORWARD_NONE but is not\n        // the same as the old config. This is not possible in current code.\n        Log.wtf(\"Adding multicast configuration on null interface?\");\n    }\n\nbut if this really can\u0027t happen, then maybe this is fine.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 187,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 187,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "d9fb65e524623995d5dba0a27b0b2e9a06e39b05",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
